{"core": "Drive pushes toward a target by converting feeling into forward motion. In Discipline, it works on the practice of steady, solitary tending — the part that holds a course through repetition without applause. Overdone, force outruns the practice: each routine gets accelerated before it has settled, and the pushing replaces the tending. The pace produces motion but nothing accumulates.", "sheetLine": "The engine keeps revving; nothing has time to become a habit."}
